{"path":"memory/allocator/max_size","title":"std::allocator<T>::max_size","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::allocator&lt;T&gt;::</span>max_size","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/allocator/max_size","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"Returns the maximum theoretically possible value of n, for which the call allocate(n, 0) could succeed.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n</tbody>\n<tbody class=\"t-dcl-rev\">\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">size_type max_size<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">throw</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx11\">(until C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11 t-until-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">size_type max_size<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark\">(deprecated in C++17)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(removed in C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns the maximum theoretically possible value of <code>n</code>, for which the call <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator/allocate\">allocate</a></span><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span>n, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> could succeed. \n</p><p>In most implementations, this returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>size_type<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> sizeof<span class=\"br0\">(</span>value_type<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The maximum supported allocation size.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits/max_size\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>max_size</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the maximum object size supported by the allocator <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function of <code>std::allocator_traits&lt;Alloc&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/allocator","title":"std::allocator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::allocator<T>::max_size","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: until C++11, since C++11, until C++20. Returns the maximum theoretically possible value of n, for which the call allocate(n, 0)…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The maximum supported allocation size."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"max_size","note":"returns the maximum object size supported by the allocator"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount